/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*
 * This is the whole script in one table. Everything the script does beyond opening
 * its own window is a module, and every module stands here - nowhere else.
 *
 * One entry per module:
 *   key     a short name for the error message, nothing else depends on it
 *   name    what it is called in a message to the reader
 *   pages   the file names it works on, or null for "wherever the script runs".
 *           Checked BEFORE init is called, so a module that has nothing to do on
 *           this page costs one comparison and not a line more.
 *   toggle  the switch in the options window that turns it off, or null for the
 *           parts that always run.
 *   init    the one function that starts it. Everything else the module needs stays
 *           inside its own block further down in the file.
 *
 * The ORDER is the order they run in, and two of them care about it: the rank
 * colouring wants the skills table already standing, and the triggers want to know
 * which boxes are ours so they can keep out of them. The options window goes first
 * so that its button is there even if a module below falls over.
 *
 * Each init runs in its own net. A module that throws takes itself out and leaves
 * the others standing, and says so in the messages - that is the whole point of
 * keeping them apart.
 *
 * To add a feature: write its block at the bottom of the file, name its one entry
 * point here, and give it a tab in SETTINGS_TABS. To remove one: delete the entry
 * and the block.
 */

